{#- The same footer on every page inside the app. Quiet, and mostly there so the open
    source half is reachable from the product rather than only from the front door.

    Privacy and terms sit here rather than four legal links, which is a footer nobody
    reads. The schedule and the erasure procedure are one click on from privacy.

    They appear only once the documents are open, which they are not during the alpha —
    a link to a 404 is worse than no link. `legal_is_public()` is the same switch the
    routes themselves answer to, so the two cannot drift apart. -#}
<footer class="site-foot">
  <a href="/about">{{ t("foot.whats-built", "What's built") }}</a>
  {#- The way into Claude and ChatGPT lives here (design.md §12, 2026-09-24). It was a
      fourth door in Learn's row, where it competed with the two that carry texts; the
      foot is where a thing that is always true and rarely wanted belongs, and the banner
      on Learn does the announcing once. Only where there is a connector to offer. -#}
  {%- if connector_is_open() %}
  <a href="/connect">{{ t("foot.targum-in-your-ai", "targum in your AI") }}</a>
  {%- endif %}
  {%- if legal_is_public() %}
  <a href="/privacy">{{ t("foot.privacy", "Privacy") }}</a>
  <a href="/terms">{{ t("foot.terms", "Terms") }}</a>
  {%- endif %}
  <a href="https://github.com/DLangellotti/targum">{{ t("foot.source", "Source") }}</a>
  <span>AGPL-3.0</span>
</footer>
